## ARC: DDL and catalog prerequisites

Apply ddl/quota.sql then ddl/reservations.sql as one contiguous formal
migration. They create two tables and depend on installed workspaces plus
local_site_id()/local_cell_id() and the site/cell registries.
Current published baseline is schema 58 / 118 public tables. If nothing
lands ahead, this would be migration 59 and 120 tables. ARC must assign the
actual next number after its accepted migration queue; never renumber 58.
Recompute fresh and restored fingerprints on that exact baseline, add the
global quota policy table to scope enumeration, and admit runtime grants.
Do not reuse the historical schema-57 fingerprints as schema-58 evidence.

Borrowing is optional and disabled unless explicitly configured. Its
separate testdata/borrowing.sql is not part of this minimal package.
Activation of borrowing needs that follow-on migration and its own acceptance.
Do not seed a synthetic quota allocation or infer cell capacity at startup.
Keep pre-cutover physical holds drained or explicitly reconciled before activation.

## TRN: exact transaction hooks

scheduling.ReserveQueuedWithin(ctx, q, attempt, intent, domain, reader)
returns (bool, error). q is the existing borrowed PostgreSQL READ COMMITTED
owner transaction; no second commit owner is created.

Implement schedulingWorkspacesWithin and schedulingEntriesWithin in the
training owner, plus initial nextFairCandidateWithin on the selected
read-only REPEATABLE READ PostgreSQL snapshot. Resolve current installed
tenant, local cell, active Workspace and requester authority. Read the
complete eligible domain, not the display pagination. Priority remains
zero until an authorized persisted class mapping exists.

In reserveDispatchWithin retain the savepoint and physical GPU acquisition;
call ReserveQueuedWithin before Nodes.QueueTrainingWithin. The complete
reader runs after scheduling locks and uses its provided executor.
Commit the hold, dequeue, physical lease, task, attempt and audit together.
Use the schema-58 audit owner path and serving principal; the fixture is
not proof that old direct audit SQL works under the new production trigger.

False/nil means exact held replay: reread owner state and enqueue no task.
Unknown commit publishes no success; retry from persisted owner state.
Queue/quota waits roll back the savepoint before persisting wait state.
Scope, malformed state, stale identity and storage errors roll back the
whole transaction without changing owner revisions.

Queued cancellation creates no hold. Preparing/running cancellation retains
its hold until the exact positive stop proof is accepted. Call ReleaseWithin
beside physical release in RecordStop, and only in ReconcileNext's proven
NeverDelivered branch. Missing post-cutover holds are integrity failures.
Foreign site/cell rows must be rejected before any owner wait/failure update.

